As I mentioned we have a mine site that is going into care and maintenance and we want to improve autonomous hybrid drone-based surveillance to guard against intruders and theft around specific perimeters at night time in particular.  
 
I am particularly interested in a hybrid fuel (or gasoline-only?) drone (fixed wing or helio ?) to maximise nocturnal flight time - although it could be an option to have alternative drones being swapped in and out of service to allow refueling etc.  We do have cellular signal with local WiFi and Starlinks at the main central areas but not at perimeters.   The objective is to remotely and autonomously patrol exterior areas using AI to pick up signs of intruders.  We would then trigger deployment of a hands-on response team including a regular drone for up close imaging and tracking of any culprits.  
 
Onboard AI can make this more autonomous and alert based which would greatly simplify our workload and focus our attentions on the ground.   This means potentially programming flight routes (may not be required if we have sufficient altitude) and identifying people movement around perimeter areas (the boundaries are not fenced so there is open access over rough terrain including sometimes heavy vegetation).  This link will give you the location and an idea of the terrain. 
 
 
